==Trivia==
*The [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]] in [[Revival of Origin]]'s background may be a reference to various fictional "[[wikipedia:Tree of life|trees of life]]", such as:
**[[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]] from Norse mythology, as [[Urs & Fenrir (Enemy)|Fenrir]] is directly named after [[wikipedia:Fenrir|Fenrir]] from Norse mythology, and Urs and [[Ultima Beast Naala]] may both be based on figures with connections to Yggdrasil: Urs (ウルス ''Urusu'') may be named after [[wikipedia:Urðr|Urðr]] (ウルズ ''Uruzu''), who lives beneath and tends to Yggdrasil, while Naala may be based on [[wikipedia:Eikþyrnir|Eikþyrnir]], who eats from [[wikipedia:Læraðr|Læraðr]]—a tree often identified with Yggdrasil. The dew that drips from Eikþyrnir's glowing antlers flows into [[wikipedia:Hvergelmir|Hvergelmir]], one of the wellsprings at Yggdrasil's roots, creating rivers that sustain life. Revival of Origin's [[Squire Rel]] or [[Sir Rel]] may also represent [[wikipedia:Ratatoskr|Ratatoskr]], a messenger squirrel who runs up and down Yggdrasil.
**The [[wikia:Mana:Tree of Mana|Tree of Mana]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Mana (series)|Mana]]'' series, as [[Zero Luza]]'s description mentions energy that makes up all things, much like [[wikia:Mana:Mana (element)|Mana]] itself, and an ancient god appears from the tree in the Uncanny Legends ending, possibly an equivalent to the [[wikia:Mana:Mana Goddess|Mana Goddess]]. This god is implied to be [[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]], who may represent ''[[wikipedia:Legend of Mana|Legend of Mana]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s final boss, the corrupted Mana Goddess.
**The [[wikia:dragonball:Tree of Might|Tree of Might]] from ''[[wikia:dragonball:Dragon Ball Z: The Tree of Might|Dragon Ball Z: The Tree of Might]]'', as both Sacred Forest and the Tree of Might have the kanji 神 ("divine") in their Japanese names, and one of the only groups that can eat its fruit are the universal deities called the [[wikia:dragonball:Kai|Kais]], again possibly tying into the ancient god mentioned in the Uncanny Legends ending.
**The [[wikia:dragonball:Universe Tree|Universe Tree]] introduced in [[wikia:dragonball:Dragon Ball Heroes|''Dragon Ball Heroes'']], as Uncanny Legends is followed by [[A Whole New World]], which features an [[Metafilibuster (Enemy)|enemy]] based on one of the [[wikia:dragonball:Universe Creation Planners|Universe Creation Planners]].
*[[Revival of Origin/Invasion|Revival of Origin Invasion]] and [[The Face of God/Invasion|The Face of God Invasion]] are the only Uncanny Legends stages to have [[Base Barrier]]s.
*Revival of Origin Invasion is the first non-[[Zero Legends]] stage and only Uncanny Legends stage to have a [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy.

